# Participants Sheet

::summary
The thread participants sheet: member rows with role meta, Surfy as a first-class agent participant. READ-ONLY in v1 — membership editing is an owner/admin action; conversation membership is the ONLY access boundary in the messages architecture.
::

::modal[name=participants title="Participants" width=300 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=login state=readonly href=#]
K. Brady Davis
Owner
:::

:::row[icon=login state=readonly href=#]
Danny Pappageorge
Member
:::

:::row[icon=surfy-fin state=readonly href=#]
Surfy
Agent — replies in the thread
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. The member rows carry `icon=login` as a person stand-in only — the intended treatment is an initials avatar (KD, DP) per the mockup's avatar-chip anatomy; rows take no avatar attr, so the stand-in stays in markup and this note carries the intent. Surfy keeps `icon=surfy-fin` — the fin IS its avatar.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
